{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P15309","uniProtkbId":"PPAP_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Prostatic acid phosphatase"},"shortNames":[{"value":"PAP"}],"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10506173"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15280042"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8132635"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9584846"}],"value":"3.1.3.2"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"5'-nucleotidase"},"shortNames":[{"value":"5'-NT"}],"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q8CE08"}],"value":"3.1.3.5"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:125"}],"value":"Acid phosphatase 3"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Ecto-5'-nucleotidase"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"}],"value":"Protein tyrosine phosphatase ACP3"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"}],"value":"3.1.3.48"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Thiamine monophosphatase"},"shortNames":[{"value":"TMPase"}]}],"contains":[{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"PAPf39"}}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:125"}],"value":"ACP3"},"synonyms":[{"value":"ACPP"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10506173"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15280042"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8132635"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9584846"}],"value":"A non-specific tyrosine phosphatase that dephosphorylates a diverse number of substrates under acidic conditions (pH 4-6) including alkyl, aryl, and acyl orthophosphate monoesters and phosphorylated proteins (PubMed:10506173, PubMed:15280042, PubMed:20498373, PubMed:9584846, PubMed:8132635). Has lipid phosphatase activity and inactivates lysophosphatidic acid in seminal plasma (PubMed:10506173, PubMed:15280042)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q8CE08"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"}],"value":"Tyrosine phosphatase that acts as a tumor suppressor of prostate cancer through dephosphorylation of ERBB2 and deactivation of MAPK-mediated signaling (PubMed:20498373). In addition to its tyrosine phosphatase activity has ecto-5'-nucleotidase activity in dorsal root ganglion (DRG) neurons. Generates adenosine from AMP which acts as a pain suppressor (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 2"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18083097"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19403677"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19451623"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19897482"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21677644"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Forms amyloid beta-sheet fibrils in semen. These fibrils, termed SEVI (semen-derived enhancer of viral infection) capture HIV virions, attach them to target cells and enhance infection (PubMed:18083097, PubMed:19451623, PubMed:19897482). SEVI amyloid fibrils are degraded by polyphenol epigallocatechin-3-gallate (EGCG), a constituent of green tea (PubMed:19451623). Assembly of SEVI amyloid fibrils and their amplification of HIV infection is inhibited by WW61, a non-natural hexapeptide inhibitor (Trp-His-Lys-chAla-Trp-hydroxyTic) (PubMed:21677644). The target cell attachment and enhancement of HIV infection is also inhibited by surfen (PubMed:19897482). Also similarly boosts XMRV (xenotropic murine leukemia virus-related virus) infection (PubMed:19403677)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"PAPf39"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Isoform 1","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"17638863"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Isoform 2","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17638863"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17897319"}],"value":"Appears to shuttle between the cell membrane and intracellular vesicles. Colocalizes with FLOT1 at cell membrane and in intracellular vesicles (PubMed:17638863). Colocalizes with LAMP2 on the lysosome membrane (PubMed:17897319)"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17638863"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17897319"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"}],"value":"Cell membrane","id":"SL-0039"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"value":"Single-pass type I membrane protein","id":"SL-9905"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17638863"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17897319"}],"value":"Lysosome membrane","id":"SL-0157"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"value":"Single-pass type I membrane protein","id":"SL-9905"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"}],"value":"Nucleus","id":"SL-0191"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20498373"}],"value":"Cytoplasm, cytosol","id":"SL-0091"}}]}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":32,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id"